Z||000000||mrfixit58||11-08-2001||04:11 PM||||Does anyone know if there is a company that makes 1.6:1 or 1.7:1 ratio rocker arms for the 3800? Specifically something around 1988 vintage?<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||11-08-2001||04:57 PM||||I know of 1:9 for the series ll supercharged. Don't know if they would work on other models.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric_PA||11-08-2001||05:17 PM||||I just got finished doing a performance rebuild on a 1990 3800 and I could not find roller rockers anywhere. I had the machine shop looking for them, but with no luck. There was an option for me though, If I wanted to spend a whole lot of money. I was told that they could modify the heads to accept ford roller rockers. I don't know how it would be done, but was told this by the shop. Also I beleive that the valve covers would be in the way. If you ever find any I would be interested.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||11-08-2001||05:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfixit58:<BR><B>Does anyone know if there is a company that makes 1.6:1 or 1.7:1 ratio rocker arms for the 3800? Specifically something around 1988 vintage?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have been looking for 3800 performance parts as well...<BR>I can find  some stuff, but $250 per piston seems a little steep?<BR>They are nothing wild, just flat top pistons...<BR>Another company wanted $400 for the same piston, a flat top 10:1 compression forged piston...<BR>I find many cam grinders have good grinds for the 3800, why not stick with the stock arm and replace the bump stick?<BR>They also had hyd. roller cams stocked...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||erikred||11-08-2001||06:08 PM||||I am not up to snuff on the Buick v6, but shouldn't some of the many parts for the 3.8 and Buick v8s also work on the 3800? There has to be roller rockers for the 3.8. Maybe you could change the head to 3.8 and use 3.8 parts?<P>Erik-||||reg||1
